#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:16
msgid "Run the default app from the `blender-bin` flake:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:22
msgid "Run a non-default app from the `blender-bin` flake:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:28
msgid ""
"Tip: you can find apps provided by this flake by running `nix flake show "
"blender-bin`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:31
msgid "Run `vim` from the `nixpkgs` flake:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:37
msgid ""
"Note that `vim` (as of the time of writing of this page) is not an app but a "
"package. Thus, Nix runs the eponymous file from the `vim` package."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:41
msgid "Run `vim` with arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:47
msgid "Run the default app from the current directory with arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:53
msgid ""
"Note: The first positional argument is always treated as the _installable_, "
"even after `--`. To pass arguments to the default installable, specify it "
"explicitly: `nix run . -- arg1 arg2` or `nix run -- . arg1 arg2`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:57
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:59
msgid ""
"`nix run` builds and runs [_installable_](./nix.md#installables), which must "
"evaluate to an _app_ or a regular Nix derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:62
msgid ""
"If _installable_ evaluates to an _app_ (see below), it executes the program "
"specified by the app definition."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:65
msgid ""
"If _installable_ evaluates to a derivation, it will try to execute the "
"program `<out>/bin/<name>`, where _out_ is the primary output store path of "
"the derivation, and _name_ is the first of the following that exists:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:70
msgid "The `meta.mainProgram` attribute of the derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:71
msgid "The `pname` attribute of the derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:72
msgid "The name part of the value of the `name` attribute of the derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:74
msgid ""
"For instance, if `name` is set to `hello-1.10`, `nix run` will run `$out/bin/"
"hello`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:77
msgid "Flake output attributes"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:79
msgid ""
"If no flake output attribute is given, `nix run` tries the following flake "
"output attributes:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:82
msgid "`apps.<system>.default`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:84
msgid "`packages.<system>.default`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:86
msgid ""
"If an attribute _name_ is given, `nix run` tries the following flake output "
"attributes:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:89
msgid "`apps.<system>.<name>`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:91
msgid "`packages.<system>.<name>`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:93
msgid "`legacyPackages.<system>.<name>`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:95
msgid "Apps"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:97
msgid ""
"An app is specified by a flake output attribute named `apps.<system>."
"<name>`. It looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:100
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"apps.x86_64-linux.blender_2_79 = {\n"
"  type = \"app\";\n"
"  program = \"${self.packages.x86_64-linux.blender_2_79}/bin/blender\";\n"
"  meta.description = \"Run Blender, a free and open-source 3D creation suite."
"\";\n"
"};\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:108
msgid "The only supported attributes are:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:110
msgid "`type` (required): Must be set to `app`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:112
msgid ""
"`program` (required): The full path of the executable to run. It must reside "
"in the Nix store."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.md:115
msgid "`meta.description` (optional): A description of the app."
msgstr ""

